Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||05-29-2001||10:39 AM||||Sorry but I don't have Ross's address but I<BR>can give you the address of the shop that is doing my 10:1 comp 3.2. They are the ones that ordered the pistons and they can tell you all about them.  <A HREF="http://www.precisionenginerebuilders.com" TARGET=_blank>www.precisionenginerebuilders.com</A> <BR>Tell-em I sent ya'<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTZ34||05-29-2001||11:19 AM||||Here is Ross' website -  <A HREF="http://www.rosspistons.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rosspistons.com/</A> <P>Not to confuse the topic... and in no particular order, take your pick.  Machine shops get incentives (discounts) for going with a preferred vendor for custom pistons so each will have their own 'recommended' brand.<P> <A HREF="http://www.jepistons.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jepistons.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.wiseco.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wiseco.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.kb-silvolite.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kb-silvolite.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ariaspistons.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ariaspistons.com/</A> <P>(Federal Mogul) <A HREF="http://216.148.221.124/" TARGET=_blank>http://216.148.221.124/</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||3
